					<!--Content starts here-->
					<tr>
						<td style="padding:20px;" valign="top"><div style="width:100%; max-width:560px; display:block;">
								<table width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" border="0">
									<tr>
										<td align="center" valign="top"><!--[if (gte mso 9)|(IE)]>
			<table width="560" align="center" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
			    <tr>
			        <td valign="top">
			<![endif]-->
											
											<table class="container" width="100%" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" style="max-width: 560px;" bgcolor="#FFFFFF" border="0">
												<tr>
													<td align="center" valign="top" style="vertical-align: top; font-size: 0;"><!--[if (gte mso 9)|(IE)]>
			            <table width="100%" align="center" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
			                <tr>
			                    <td valign="top">
			            <![endif]-->
														
														<div style="max-width: 358px; display: inline-block; vertical-align: top;">
															<table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
																<tr>
																	<td align="left" valign="top" style="padding-right:20px;"><table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" bgcolor="#FFFFFF">
																			<tr>
																				<td align="left" valign="top"><div style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:20px; text-align:left; color:#231f20;"><font style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:20px; text-align:left; color:#231f20;"> As someone who was recently diagnosed with epilepsy, there is a lot of information you've been asked to quickly absorb. We know that it can be a lot to take in and it's important to be sure you fully understand your diagnosis to help you stay safe and better manage your condition.<br />
																						<br />
																						Here is our Epilepsy 101, to be sure you're up-to-speed on the basics of epilepsy:<br />
																						<br />
																						</font></div></td>
																			</tr>
																			<tr>
																				<td align="left" valign="top"><div style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color:#231f20; font-size:16px; line-height:22px; font-weight:bold;"><font style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:22px; color:#231f20; font-weight:bold;">What is epilepsy?</font></div></td>
																			</tr>
																			<tr>
																				<td align="left" valign="top"><div style="height:12px; line-height:12px;"><img src="http://www.myhealthnewsletter.com/orlandohealth/neuro/epilepsy/Email-1/images/spacer.gif" width="100%" height="12" alt="" border="0" style="display:block;" /></div></td>
																			</tr>
																			<tr>
																				<td align="left" valign="top"><div style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color:#231f20; font-size:16px; line-height:22px;"><font style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:22px; color:#231f20;">Epilepsy is a neurological condition, meaning it affects the brain. It may also be known as a "seizure disorder". Most people diagnosed with epilepsy have typically experienced two or more seizures.</font></div></td>
																			</tr>
																			<tr>
																				<td align="left" valign="top"><img src="http://www.myhealthnewsletter.com/orlandohealth/neuro/epilepsy/Email-1/images/spacer.gif" width="100%" height="20" alt="" border="0" style="display:block;" /></td>
																			</tr>
																			<tr>
																				<td align="left" valign="top"><div style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color:#231f20; font-size:16px; line-height:22px; font-weight:bold;"><font style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:22px; color:#231f20; font-weight:bold;">What is a seizure?</font></div></td>
																			</tr>
																			<tr>
																				<td align="left" valign="top"><div style="height:12px; line-height:12px;"><img src="http://www.myhealthnewsletter.com/orlandohealth/neuro/epilepsy/Email-1/images/spacer.gif" width="100%" height="12" alt="" border="0" style="display:block;" /></div></td>
																			</tr>
																			<tr>
																				<td align="left" valign="top"><div style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color:#231f20; font-size:16px; line-height:22px;"><font style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:22px; color:#231f20;">You've likely experienced at least one seizure prior to your diagnosis. A seizure is a temporary change in behavior caused by a burst of abnormal electrical activity in the brain. The exact appearance of a seizure may vary depending on the area of the brain affected. Seizures typically last between a few seconds and a few minutes.</font></div></td>
																			</tr>
																			<tr>
																				<td align="left" valign="top"><img src="http://www.myhealthnewsletter.com/orlandohealth/neuro/epilepsy/Email-1/images/spacer.gif" width="100%" height="20" alt="" border="0" style="display:block;" /></td>
																			</tr>
																			<tr>
																				<td align="left" valign="top"><table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
																						<tr>
																							<td align="left" valign="top" colspan="2"><div style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color:#231f20; font-size:16px; line-height:22px; font-weight:bold;"><font style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:22px; color:#231f20; font-weight:bold;">What are the common treatments for epilepsy?</font></div></td>
																						</tr>
																						<tr>
																							<td align="left" valign="top" colspan="2"><div style="height:12px; line-height:12px;"><img src="http://www.myhealthnewsletter.com/orlandohealth/neuro/epilepsy/Email-1/images/spacer.gif" width="100%" height="12" alt="" border="0" style="display:block;" /></div></td>
																						</tr>
																						<tr>
																							<td align="left" valign="top"><img src="http://www.myhealthnewsletter.com/orlandohealth/neuro/epilepsy/Email-1/images/bullet.jpg" alt="" width="30" height="22" border="0" style="display:block;" /></td>
																							<td align="left" valign="top"><div style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color:#231f20; font-size:16px; line-height:22px;" class="outlook_br"><font style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:22px; color:#231f20;"><span style="font-weight:bold;">Medication.</span> Medications are effective at limiting the spread of seizures in the brain for about two-thirds of people with epilepsy.</font></div></td>
																						</tr>
																						<tr>
																							<td align="left" valign="top" colspan="2"><div style="height:7px; line-height:7px;"><img src="http://www.myhealthnewsletter.com/orlandohealth/neuro/epilepsy/Email-1/images/spacer.gif" width="100%" height="7" alt="" border="0" style="display:block;" /></div></td>
																						</tr>
																						<tr>
																							<td align="left" valign="top"><img src="http://www.myhealthnewsletter.com/orlandohealth/neuro/epilepsy/Email-1/images/bullet.jpg" alt="" width="30" height="22" border="0" style="display:block;" /></td>
																							<td align="left" valign="top"><div style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color:#231f20; font-size:16px; line-height:22px;" class="outlook_br"><font style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:22px; color:#231f20;"><span style="font-weight:bold;">Surgery.</span> If seizures are centered in a single area of the brain, surgery may be an option.</font></div></td>
																						</tr>
																						<tr>
																							<td align="left" valign="top" colspan="2"><div style="height:7px; line-height:7px;"><img src="http://www.myhealthnewsletter.com/orlandohealth/neuro/epilepsy/Email-1/images/spacer.gif" width="100%" height="7" alt="" border="0" style="display:block;" /></div></td>
																						</tr>
																						<tr>
																							<td align="left" valign="top"><img src="http://www.myhealthnewsletter.com/orlandohealth/neuro/epilepsy/Email-1/images/bullet.jpg" alt="" width="30" height="22" border="0" style="display:block;" /></td>
																							<td align="left" valign="top"><div style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color:#231f20; font-size:16px; line-height:22px;" class="outlook_br"><font style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:22px; color:#231f20;"><span style="font-weight:bold;">Other treatments.</span> If medication and surgery are not effective, there are other treatments that your physician can prescribe to help. This could include prescribing a specific diet or using other medical treatments such as using a device to send electrical signals to a nerve.</font></div></td>
																						</tr>
																						<tr>
																							<td align="left" valign="top" colspan="2"><img src="http://www.myhealthnewsletter.com/orlandohealth/neuro/epilepsy/Email-1/images/spacer.gif" width="100%" height="20" alt="" border="0" style="display:block;" /></td>
																						</tr>
																					</table></td>
																			</tr>
																			<tr>
																				<td align="left" valign="top"><div style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color:#231f20; font-size:16px; line-height:22px; font-weight:bold;" class="outlook_br"><font style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:22px; color:#231f20; font-weight:bold;">How can I help manage my epilepsy?</font></div></td>
																			</tr>
																			<tr>
																				<td align="left" valign="top"><div style="height:12px; line-height:12px;"><img src="http://www.myhealthnewsletter.com/orlandohealth/neuro/epilepsy/Email-1/images/spacer.gif" width="100%" height="12" alt="" border="0" style="display:block;" /></div></td>
																			</tr>
																			<tr>
																				<td align="left" valign="top"><table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0">
																						<tr>
																							<td align="left" valign="top"><img src="http://www.myhealthnewsletter.com/orlandohealth/neuro/epilepsy/Email-1/images/bullet.jpg" alt="" width="30" height="22" border="0" style="display:block;" /></td>
																							<td align="left" valign="top"><div style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color:#231f20; font-size:16px; line-height:22px;" class="outlook_br"><font style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:22px; color:#231f20;">Ask your doctor any questions you may have.</font></div></td>
																						</tr>
																						<tr>
																							<td align="left" valign="top" colspan="2"><div style="height:7px; line-height:7px;"><img src="http://www.myhealthnewsletter.com/orlandohealth/neuro/epilepsy/Email-1/images/spacer.gif" width="100%" height="7" alt="" border="0" style="display:block;" /></div></td>
																						</tr>
																						<tr>
																							<td align="left" valign="top"><img src="http://www.myhealthnewsletter.com/orlandohealth/neuro/epilepsy/Email-1/images/bullet.jpg" alt="" width="30" height="22" border="0" style="display:block;" /></td>
																							<td align="left" valign="top"><div style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color:#231f20; font-size:16px; line-height:22px;" class="outlook_br"><font style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:22px; color:#231f20;">Be sure to get enough sleep.</font></div></td>
																						</tr>
																						<tr>
																							<td align="left" valign="top" colspan="2"><div style="height:7px; line-height:7px;"><img src="http://www.myhealthnewsletter.com/orlandohealth/neuro/epilepsy/Email-1/images/spacer.gif" width="100%" height="7" alt="" border="0" style="display:block;" /></div></td>
																						</tr>
																						<tr>
																							<td align="left" valign="top"><img src="http://www.myhealthnewsletter.com/orlandohealth/neuro/epilepsy/Email-1/images/bullet.jpg" alt="" width="30" height="22" border="0" style="display:block;" /></td>
																							<td align="left" valign="top"><div style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color:#231f20; font-size:16px; line-height:22px;" class="outlook_br"><font style="font-family:Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size:16px; line-height:22px; color:#231f20;">Keep a journal of your seizures.</font></div></td>
																						</tr>
																						<tr>
																							<td align="left" valign="top" colspan="2"><div style="height:7px; line-height:7px;"><img src="http://www.myhealthnewsletter.com/orlandohealth/neuro/epilepsy/Email-1/images/spacer.gif" width="100%" height="7" alt="" border="0" style="display:block;" /></div></td>
																						</tr>
																						<tr>
																							<td align="left" valign="top"><img src="http://www.myhealthnewsletter.com/orlandohealth/neuro/epilepsy/Email-1/images/bullet.jpg" alt="" width="30" height="22" border="0" style="display:block;" /></td>
